  "title": "Building Codes and Amendments - Douglas County",
  "text": "Building Codes and Amendments - Douglas County\nAlert\nBy order of Sheriff Darren Weekly,\nStage 1 Fire Restrictions\nare in place for unincorporated areas of Douglas County as of Aug. 20, 2026.\nYour County\nService Finder\nElected Officials\nJobs\nOffices, Departments & Divisions\nVolunteer Opportunities\nLiving\nMental Health\nMental Health Collaborative\nMental Health Resources\nDriving\nDriver License\nVehicle Registration\nMy Property\nOpen Data / Dougco Hub\nPermits (Building)\nTaxes\nValue\nAssistance\nFinancial\nFood\nMedical\nOnline Resource Search\nRoadways\nGravel Roads\nTransportation Projects\nSnow and Ice Removal\nTraffic\nGetting Outdoors\nParks, Trails, Historic Resources and Open Space Fund\nDecode DC Outdoors\nOpen Space Properties & Trails\nParks\nRueter-Hess Recreation\nHealthy Living\nCommunity Health and Clinical Services\nDisease Surveillance\nEmergency Preparedness and Response\nEnvironmental Health\nVital Records\nRequest/File Documents\nColorado Open Records Act (CORA)\nMarriage / Civil Union Licenses\nPassports\nBusiness\nMy Property\nCommercial Forms\nCommercial Property\nProperty Tax\nResources\nEconomic Development\nEconomic Development Reports\nOpen Data / Dougco Hub\nPopulation & Development Report\nNews\nMedia Contacts / PIOs\nVolunteer Opportunities\nContact Us\nAsk a Question, Report Issues or Concerns\nKey Contacts\nMedia Contacts / PIOs\nStay Connected\nMenu\n☰\nBuilding Division\nBuilding Codes and Amendments\nDesign Information\nOver the Counter Plan Review\nContractor Registration\nInspections\nPermits\nWildfire Awareness\nBe Prepared for Wildfires\nBe Proactive: Community Wildfire Protection\nBe a Partner in Wildfire Prevention\nLooking for something specific?\nService Finder\n×\n01.\nHelp Me With...\nSelect from list\nMy Residential Property\nMy Driver's License or Vehicle Registration\nRequesting Assistance\nElections\nHealth Department\n02.\nSelect from list\nMy Property Valuation\nUnderstanding My Valuation\nPaying My Property Tax\nNeighborhood Sales\nBuilding Permits\nVehicle Registration - New Stickers\nVehicle Registration - New Vehicle\nDrivers License - New or Renew\nNew Resident Vehicle Registration\nAdult Protection\nChild Welfare\nChild Support\nChild Care\nFinancial Assistance\nMedical Assistance\nFood Assistance\nRegister to Vote / Update Voter Registration\nUpcoming Election Information\nBallot Drop Box Locations\nVoter Service and Polling Centers\nBirth/Death Records\nRestaurant Inspections\nCommunity Health\nChild Care Center Inspections\nSeptic System Inspections\nEmergency Preparedness & Response\nDisease Surveillance\nMental and Behavioral Health Education\nCommunity Health and Clinical Services\nWomen, Infants and Children\n03.\n×\n× Close\nLiving\nMental Health\nMental Health Collaborative\nMental Health Resources\nDriving\nDriver License\nVehicle Registration\nMy Property\nOpen Data / Dougco Hub\nPermits (Building)\nTaxes\nValue\nAssistance\nFinancial\nFood\nMedical\nOnline Resource Search\nRoadways\nGravel Roads\nTransportation Projects\nSnow and Ice Removal\nTraffic\nGetting Outdoors\nParks, Trails, Historic Resources and Open Space Fund\nDecode DC Outdoors\nOpen Space Properties & Trails\nParks\nRueter-Hess Recreation\nHealthy Living\nCommunity Health and Clinical Services\nDisease Surveillance\nEmergency Preparedness and Response\nEnvironmental Health\nVital Records\nRequest/File Documents\nColorado Open Records Act (CORA)\nMarriage / Civil Union Licenses\nPassports\nBusiness\nMy Property\nCommercial Forms\nCommercial Property\nProperty Tax\nResources\nEconomic Development\nEconomic Development Reports\nOpen Data / Dougco Hub\nPopulation & Development Report\nNews\nMedia Contacts / PIOs\nVolunteer Opportunities\nContact Us\nAsk a Question, Report Issues or Concerns\nKey Contacts\nMedia Contacts / PIOs\nStay Connected\nBuilding Division\nBuilding Codes and Amendments\nDesign Information\nOver the Counter Plan Review\nContractor Registration\nInspections\nPermits\nWildfire Awareness\nBe Prepared for Wildfires\nBe Proactive: Community Wildfire Protection\nBe a Partner in Wildfire Prevention\nBuilding Codes and Amendments\nAdopted Codes\nThe following Codes with Amendments have been adopted by the Board of Douglas County Commissioners.\n2023 National Electrical Code\nClick here to view the Amendments to the\n2023 National Electric Code\n.\nBuilding Codes - Adopted on July 01, 2026, adopted amendments to the Douglas County Building Codes effective July 1, 2026. NEC effective date will be January 1, 2027\nBy\nclicking here,\nyou can view the 2024 Douglas County amendments\nTable of Contents\nExhibit A  – Amendments Common to all Adopted Codes\n2024 International Residential Code (IRC) Amendments\n2024 International Building Code (IBC) Amendments\n2024 International Plumbing Code (IPC) Amendments\n2024 International Mechanical Code (IMC) Amendments\n2024 International Fuel Gas Code (IFGC) Amendments\n2024 International Energy Conservation Code (IECC) Amendments\n2024 International Swimming Pool and Spa Code (ISPSC) Amendments\n2023 National Electrical Code (NEC) Amendments\nExhibit B Wildfire Mitigation Standards\nExhibit C Standard for Water Supplies for Rural Fire Fighting\nExhibit D Installation Standards for Potable Water Storage Tanks and Cisterns for Domestic Use IS-22-98\nExhibit E 2024 IBC Appendix Chapter Q Section Q-1205 Solar Photovoltaic Power Systems\nExhibit F Colorado Model Electric Ready and Solar Ready Code\n2024 International Fire Code\nAdopted July 14, 2026,\n2024\nInternational Fire Code (IFC) as amended as Ordinance No. O-026-004\n.\nColorado Safety Code for Elevators & Escalators and Standard for Platform Lifts and Stairway Chair Lifts\nEffective June 27, 2023, the Douglas County Board of County Commissioners adopted a\nResolution Approving\nRevisions to State Safety Code for; Elevators and Escalators (ASME A17.1-2019), Platform Lifts and Stairway Chair Lifts (ASME A18.1-2017), Existing Elevators and Escalators (ASME A17.3-2005), and Automated People Movers (ASCE 21-2013).\nApproved AHJ Program Requirements Notice\nColorado Division of Oil and Public Safety Conveyance Regulations\n(Effective January 1, 2026)\nDouglas County Wildfire Resiliency Code\nAdopted July 01, 2026,\nDouglas County Wildfire Resiliency Code\n2025 Colorado Wildfire Resiliency Code Map\nBuilding Division Phone:\n303-660-7497\nBuilding Division Location:\n100 Third Street\nCastle Rock, CO 80104\nGoogle Map\nEmail Building Division:\nContact Us\nOur Office Locations\nGeneral Info\n303-660-7400\nLooking for\nAccessibility Statement\nConnect with Douglas County\nCopyright © 2026 Douglas County Government |\nAccessibility Statement\n|\nPrivacy Policy\nby Webolutions Digital Marketing Agency",
